From f431dca7b2996b92e1e998ecc12465dc9bfc74df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaVector1 <DeltaVector1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 10:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] Bound the rollout HTTP timeouts; they were starving the
 engines

verifiers' build_async_openai left the OpenAI SDK defaults in place:
connect=5.0s, read=600s. Both are wrong for a link with 217 ms of round trip
and 10-33% packet loss.

read=600s is the expensive one. The orchestrator runs a fixed number of
rollouts in flight, so a wedged request holds one of those slots for ten
minutes. That is what "121 in flight while the engines ran 3 between them"
was: most of the in-flight count was dead requests waiting out this timeout
while the engines starved behind them. Now 300s, which still leaves wide
margin over a 54.6s mean and 87.8s p90 generation.

connect=5s cannot survive a lost SYN: the retransmits alone wait 1s, 2s, 4s.
Now 30s. Both are overridable through PRIME_ROLLOUT_TIMEOUT_S and
PRIME_ROLLOUT_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_S.

config.py was not mounted, so it is extracted from the image and added to the
orchestrator mounts in cluster.sh. Checked first that no local copy existed;
extracting a file that does have local changes is how _FiniteGrad was lost.
Verified by importing the edited module in the running container's package
context: Timeout(connect=30.0, read=300.0, write=300.0, pool=30.0).

apply_at_step.sh takes CHECK_FILE so its pre-flight guard can verify a mount
rather than only a config value.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wiESxhziDrnsLnG9aizTd
---
 scripts/china/apply_at_step.sh                |  10 +-
 scripts/china/cluster.sh                      |   1 +
 .../verifiers/verifiers/v1/clients/config.py  | 155 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 162 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 source/deps/verifiers/verifiers/v1/clients/config.py

diff --git a/scripts/china/apply_at_step.sh b/scripts/china/apply_at_step.sh
index 5b41595..1f2d2ac 100755
--- a/scripts/china/apply_at_step.sh
+++ b/scripts/china/apply_at_step.sh
@@ -18,7 +18,8 @@ STEP=${STEP:?set STEP -- the step number to wait for}
 TAG=${CONFIG_TAG:?set CONFIG_TAG}
 RUN=${RUN:?set RUN}
 RUN_NAME=${RUN_NAME:?set RUN_NAME}
-EXPECT=${EXPECT:-}          # optional "key = value" line to verify in the config
+EXPECT=${EXPECT:-}          # optional literal text to verify before arming
+CHECK_FILE=${CHECK_FILE:-}  # file EXPECT must appear in; defaults to the orchestrator config
 GIVE_UP_HOURS=${GIVE_UP_HOURS:-6}
 INTERVAL=${INTERVAL:-60}
 DEPLOY=/data/glm52-rl/deployment
@@ -35,10 +36,11 @@ log "waiting for trainer step $STEP, then restarting the orchestrator (tag=$TAG)
 # Refuse to arm if the change is not actually staged. Restarting for nothing
 # would discard a batch and change no behaviour.
 if [ -n "$EXPECT" ]; then
-  if grep -qF -- "$EXPECT" "$CFG"; then
-    log "config check ok: '$EXPECT' present in $CFG"
+  check_in=${CHECK_FILE:-$CFG}
+  if grep -qF -- "$EXPECT" "$check_in"; then
+    log "pre-flight ok: '$EXPECT' present in $check_in"
   else
-    log "ABORT: '$EXPECT' is not in $CFG. Nothing to apply."
+    log "ABORT: '$EXPECT' is not in $check_in. Nothing to apply."
     exit 1
   fi
 fi
